// Found by a coverage-guided run of the FeasibleTargetsAreReachableWithSpilling property
// test: while the stack grows towards the tail size, dupDeepestRelevantTailSlot considers the
// JUNK at the stack bottom "required in args" (the target args contain a JUNK entry, which
// requiredInArgs matches) and, since it is not dup-reachable, tries to compress the stack --
// popping the freshly duplicated v1 that the growth just produced. Junk never needs rescuing,
// so the dup and the compress-pop undo each other until MaxIterationsReached.
